          "message": {
            "text": "Admitted raw claim fields are emitted directly to terminal output without control-character escaping, permitting terminal escape/control injection for an operator viewing claims or review queues. Also: The claims-list CLI renders source-controlled raw claim fields directly to the terminal without control-character neutralization, allowing terminal escape-sequence injection. Also: The claims-show CLI renders source-controlled raw claim fields directly to the terminal without control-character neutralization, allowing terminal escape-sequence injection. Also: The dry-run sample CLI prints source-controlled model_raw, benchmark_raw, and score_raw fields directly to the terminal without control-character neutralization, allowing terminal escape-sequence injection. Also: The review-queue CLI renders source-controlled raw claim fields directly to the terminal without control-character neutralization, allowing terminal escape-sequence injection. Additional reducer evidence: Claims list output does not neutralize persisted source-controlled raw fields. Claims show output does not neutralize persisted source-controlled fields or evidence locations. Ingestion dry-run output interpolates source-controlled model and score strings without terminal/log neutralization. Review queue output does not neutralize persisted source-controlled fields. Additional reducer summary: CLI commands emit attacker-controlled raw source and evidence strings directly to the operator terminal without control or ANSI/newline neutralization. Additional manifestation: Raw model, benchmark, and score fields are  Validated as a reportable source-level finding; no live external state was assumed."
          },
